s)\\n    * [ Jobs  ](/root/internal-api-client/-/jobs)\\n    * [ Pipeline editor  ](/root/internal-api-client/-/ci/editor?branch_name=main)\\n    * [ Pipeline schedules  ](/root/internal-api-client/-/pipeline_schedules)\\n    * [ Artifacts  ](/root/internal-api-client/-/artifacts)\\n\\n  * Secure \\n\\n    * [ Security configuration  ](/root/internal-api-client/-/security/configuration)\\n\\n  * Deploy \\n\\n    * [ Releases  ](/root/internal-api-client/-/releases)\\n    * [ Feature flags  ](/root/internal-api-client/-/feature_flags)\\n    * [ Package Registry  ](/root/internal-api-client/-/packages)\\n    * [ Model registry  ](/root/internal-api-client/-/ml/models)\\n\\n  * Operate \\n\\n    * [ Environments  ](/root/internal-api-client/-/environments)\\n    * [ Kubernetes clusters  ](/root/internal-api-client/-/clusters)\\n    * [ Terraform states  ](/root/internal-api-client/-/terraform)\\n    * [ Terraform modules  ](/root/internal-api-client/-/terraform_module_registry)\\n\\n  * Monitor \\n\\n    * [ Error Tracking  ](/root/internal-api-client/-/error_tracking)\\n    * [ Alerts  ](/root/internal-api-client/-/alert_management)\\n    * [ Incidents  ](/root/internal-api-client/-/incidents)\\n\\n  * Analyze \\n\\n    * [ Value stream analytics  ](/root/internal-api-client/-/value_stream_analytics)\\n    * [ Contributor analytics  ](/root/internal-api-client/-/graphs/main?ref_type=heads)\\n    * [ CI/CD analytics  ](/root/internal-api-client/-/pipelines/charts)\\n    * [ Repository analytics  ](/root/internal-api-client/-/graphs/main/charts)\\n    * [ Model experiments  ](/root/internal-api-client/-/ml/experiments)\\n\\n  * * * *\\n\\nSettings \\n\\n    * [ General  ](/root/internal-api-client/edit)\\n    * [ Integrations  ](/root/internal-api-client/-/settings/integrations)\\n    * [ Webhooks  ](/root/internal-api-client/-/hooks)\\n    * [ Access tokens  ](/root/internal-api-client/-/settings/access_tokens)\\n    * [ Repository  ](/root/internal-api-client/-/settings/repository)\\n    * [ Merge requests  ](/root/internal-api-client/-/settings/merge_requests)\\n    * [ CI/CD  ](/root/internal-api-client/-/settings/ci_cd)\\n    * [ Packages and registries  ](/root/internal-api-client/-/settings/packages_and_registries)\\n    * [ Monitor  ](/root/internal-api-client/-/settings/operations)\\n    * [ Usage Quotas  ](/root/internal-api-client/-/usage_quotas)\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nHelp \\n\\n  *     * [ Help  ](/help)\\n    * [ Support  ](https://about.gitlab.com/get-help/)\\n    * [ GitLab documentation  ](/help/docs)\\n    * [ Compare GitLab plans  ](https://about.gitlab.com/pricing)\\n    * [ Community forum  ](https://forum.gitlab.com)\\n    * [ Contribute to GitLab  ](/help#contribute-to-gitlab)\\n    * [ Provide feedback  ](https://about.gitlab.com/submit-feedback)\\n  *     * Keyboard shortcuts ` ? `\\n    * What\\'s new  4 \\n\\n\\n\\n[ Admin  ](http://the-agent-company.com:8929/admin)\\n\\n[ Milestones ](/dashboard/milestones) [ Snippets ](/dashboard/snippets) [ Activity ](/dashboard/activity) [ Groups ](/dashboard/groups) [ Projects ](/dashboard/projects) [ Create a new issue ](/root/internal-api-client/-/issues/new)\\n\\n<::before>\\n\\nTo help improve GitLab, we would like to periodically [ collect usage information ](/help/administration/settings/usage_statistics.md) . This can be changed at any time in [ your settings ](/admin/application_settings/metrics_and_profiling#js-usage-settings) . \\n\\n[ Send service data  ](/admin/application_settings?application_setting%5Busage_ping_enabled%5D=1&application_setting%5Bversion_check_enabled%5D=1) [ Don\\'t send service data  ](/admin/application_settings?application_setting%5Busage_ping_enabled%5D=0&application_setting%5Bversion_check_enabled%5D=0)\\n\\n  1. <::after> [ Administrator  ](/root)\\n  2. <::after> [ internal-api-client  ](/root/internal-api-client)\\n  3. [ CI/CD Settings  ](/root/internal-api-client/-/settings/ci_cd)\\n\\n\\n\\n#  CI/CD Settings \\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  General pipelines \\n\\nCustomize your pipeline configuration. \\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\n<::before><::after> Public pipelines \\n\\nAllow public access to pipelines and job details, including output logs and artifacts. [ ](/help/ci/pipelines/settings.md#change-which-users-can-view-your-pipelines)\\n\\n<::before><::after> Auto-cancel redundant pipelines \\n\\nPipelines for new changes cause older pending or running pipelines on the same branch to be cancelled. [ ](/help/ci/pipelines/settings.md#auto-cancel-redundant-pipelines)\\n\\n<::before><::after> Prevent outdated deployment jobs \\n\\nWhen a deployment job is successful, prevent older deployment jobs that are still pending. [ ](/help/ci/pipelines/settings.md#prevent-outdated-deployment-jobs)\\n\\n<::before><::after> Allow job retries for rollback deployments \\n\\nAllow job retries even if the deployment job is outdated. [ ](/help/ci/environments/deployment_safety.md#job-retries-for-rollback-deployments)\\n\\n<::before><::after> Use separate caches for protected branches \\n\\nUnprotected branches will not have access to the cache from protected branches. [ ](/help/ci/caching/index.md#cache-key-names)\\n\\nCI/CD configuration file \\n\\nThe name of the CI/CD configuration file. A path relative to the root directory is optional (for example ` my/path/.myfile.yml ` ). [ ](/help/ci/pipelines/settings.md#specify-a-custom-cicd-configuration-file)\\n\\n* * *\\n\\n#####  Git strategy \\n\\nChoose which Git strategy to use when fetching the project. [ ](/help/ci/pipelines/settings.md#choose-the-default-git-strategy)\\n\\n<::before><::after> git clone \\n\\nFor each job, clone the repository. \\n\\n<::before><::after> git fetch \\n\\nFor each job, re-use the project workspace. If the workspace doesn\\'t exist, use ` git clone ` . \\n\\nGit shallow clone \\n\\nThe number of changes to fetch from GitLab when cloning a repository. Lower values can speed up pipeline execution. Set to ` 0 ` or blank to fetch all branches and tags for each job [ ](/help/ci/pipelines/settings.md#limit-the-number-of-changes-fetched-during-clone)\\n\\n* * *\\n\\nTimeout \\n\\nJobs fail if they run longer than the timeout time. Input value is in seconds by default. Human readable input is also accepted, for example ` 1 hour ` . [ ](/help/ci/pipelines/settings.md#set-a-limit-for-how-long-jobs-can-run)\\n\\nMaximum artifacts size \\n\\nThe maximum file size in megabytes for individual job artifacts. [ ](/help/administration/settings/continuous_integration.md#maximum-artifacts-size)\\n\\nSave changes \\n\\n* * *\\n\\n####  Pipeline status \\n\\n**Pipeline status \u00b7** [ ](http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/internal-api-client/-/commits/main)\\n\\nmain \\n\\nSelect Git revision \\n\\n  * Branches  1 \\n  * main  default  protected \\n\\n\\n\\n1 result \\n\\nMarkdown \\n\\n[  ![pipeline status  ](  http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/internal-api-client/badges/main/pipeline.svg  )  ](http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/internal-api-client/-/commits/main) \\n\\n* * *\\n\\nHTML \\n\\nhref=  \"http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/internal-api-client/-/commits/main\"  > alt=  \"pipeline status\"  src=  \"http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/internal-api-client/badges/main/pipeline.svg\"  />\\n\\n* * *\\n\\nAsciiDoc \\n\\nimage:http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/internal-api-client/badges/main/pipeline.svg[link=\"http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/internal-api-client/-/commits/main\",title=\"pipeline status\"] \\n\\n####  Coverage report \\n\\n**Coverage report \u00b7** [ ](http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/internal-api-client/-/commits/main)\\n\\nmain \\n\\nSelect Git revision \\n\\n  * Branches  1 \\n  * main  default  protected \\n\\n\\n\\n1 result \\n\\nMarkdown \\n\\n[  ![coverage report  ](  http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/internal-api-client/badges/main/coverage.svg  )  ](http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/internal-api-client/-/commits/main) \\n\\n* * *\\n\\nHTML \\n\\nhref=  \"http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/internal-api-client/-/commits/main\"  > alt=  \"coverage report\"  src=  \"http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/internal-api-client/badges/main/coverage.svg\"  />\\n\\n* * *\\n\\nAsciiDoc \\n\\nimage:http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/internal-api-client/badges/main/coverage.svg[link=\"http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/internal-api-client/-/commits/main\",title=\"coverage report\"] \\n\\n####  Latest release \\n\\n**Latest release \u00b7** [ ](http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/internal-api-client/-/releases)\\n\\nmain \\n\\nSelect Git revision \\n\\n  * Branches  1 \\n  * main  default  protected \\n\\n\\n\\n1 result \\n\\nMarkdown \\n\\n[  ![Latest Release  ](  http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/internal-api-client/-/badges/release.svg  )  ](http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/internal-api-client/-/releases) \\n\\n* * *\\n\\nHTML \\n\\nhref=  \"http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/internal-api-client/-/releases\"  > alt=  \"Latest Release\"  src=  \"http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/internal-api-client/-/badges/release.svg\"  />\\n\\n* * *\\n\\nAsciiDoc \\n\\nimage:http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/internal-api-client/-/badges/release.svg[link=\"http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/internal-api-client/-/releases\",title=\"Latest Release\"] \\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  Auto DevOps \\n\\n[ Automate building, testing, and deploying ](/help/topics/autodevops/index.md) your applications based on your continuous integration and delivery configuration. [ How do I get started? ](/help/topics/autodevops/cloud_deployments/auto_devops_with_gke.md)\\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\n<::before><::after> Default to Auto DevOps pipeline  instance enabled \\n\\nThe Auto DevOps pipeline runs if no alternative CI configuration file is found. [ Learn more. ](/help/topics/autodevops/index.md)\\n\\nAdd a [ Kubernetes cluster integration ](/help/user/project/clusters/index.md) with a domain, or create an AUTO_DEVOPS_PLATFORM_TARGET CI variable. \\n\\n**Deployment strategy**\\n\\n<::before><::after> Continuous deployment to production [ ](/help/topics/autodevops/stages.md#auto-deploy)\\n\\n<::before><::after> Continuous deployment to production using timed incremental rollout [ ](/help/topics/autodevops/cicd_variables.md#timed-incremental-rollout-to-production)\\n\\n<::before><::after> Automatic deployment to staging, manual deployment to production [ ](/help/topics/autodevops/cicd_variables.md#incremental-rollout-to-production)\\n\\nSave changes \\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  Runners \\n\\nRunners are processes that pick up and execute CI/CD jobs for GitLab. [ What is GitLab Runner? ](https://docs.gitlab.com/runner/)\\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\nRegister as many runners as you want. You can register runners as separate users, on separate servers, and on your local machine. \\n\\n#####  How do runners pick up jobs? \\n\\nRunners are either: \\n\\n  * <::marker> active  \\\\- Available to run jobs. \\n  * <::marker> paused  \\\\- Not available to run jobs. \\n\\n\\n\\nTags control which type of jobs a runner can handle. By tagging a runner, you make sure runners only handle the jobs they are equipped to run. [ Learn more. ](/help/ci/runners/configure_runners.md#how-the-runner-uses-tags)\\n\\n####  Project runners \\n\\n<::before>\\n\\nThese runners are assigned to this project. \\n\\n[ New project runner  ](/root/internal-api-client/-/runners/new)\\n\\nRegister a project runner \\n\\n* Registration token \\n\\nSupport for registration tokens is deprecated \\n\\n*   * Show runner installation and registration instructions \\n\\n\\n*   * Reset registration token \\n\\n\\n\\n* * *\\n\\n####  Instance runners \\n\\n<::before>\\n\\n[ These runners ](/help/ci/runners/runners_scope.md#instance-runners) are available to all groups and projects. \\n\\nEnable instance runners for this project \\n\\nThis GitLab instance does not provide any instance runners yet. Administrators can register instance runners in the admin area. \\n\\n####  Group runners \\n\\n<::before>\\n\\nThese runners are shared across projects in this group.   \\n  \\nGroup runners can be managed with the [ Runner API ](/help/api/runners.md) . \\n\\nThis project does not belong to a group and cannot make use of group runners. \\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  Artifacts \\n\\nA job artifact is an archive of files and directories saved by a job when it finishes. \\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\nKeep artifacts from most recent successful jobs  The latest artifacts created by jobs in the most recent successful pipeline will be stored. [ Learn more. ](/help/ci/jobs/job_artifacts.md#keep-artifacts-from-most-recent-successful-jobs)\\n\\nCollapse \\n\\n##  Variables \\n\\nVariables store information that you can use in job scripts. Each project can define a maximum of 8000 variables. [ Learn more. ](/help/ci/variables/index.md)\\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\nVariables can be accidentally exposed in a job log, or maliciously sent to a third party server. The masked variable feature can help reduce the risk of accidentally exposing variable values, but is not a guaranteed method to prevent malicious users from accessing variables. [ How can I make my variables more secure? ](/help/ci/variables/index.md#cicd-variable-security)\\n\\nVariables can have several attributes. [ Learn more. ](/help/ci/variables/index.md#define-a-cicd-variable-in-the-ui)\\n\\n  * <::marker> **Visibility:** Set the visibility level for the value. Can be visible, masked, or masked and hidden. \\n  * <::marker> **Flags**\\n    * <::marker> ` Protected: ` Only exposed to protected branches or protected tags. \\n    * <::marker> ` Expanded: ` Variables with ` $ ` will be treated as the start of a reference to another variable. \\n\\n\\n\\n##  CI/CD Variables  1 \\n\\nReveal values  Add variable \\n\\nKey  \u2191  (Click to sort descending)  |  Value  |  Environments  |  Actions   \\n---|---|---|---  \\nINTERNAL_API_KEY  Protected  Expanded  |  *****  |  All (default)  |   \\n  \\n##  Edit variable \\n\\n<::after>\\n\\nType \\n\\nVariable (default) \\n\\n  *   *   * Variable (default) \\n  * File \\n  *   * \\n\\n\\nEnvironments  [ ](/help/ci/environments/index.md#limit-the-environment-scope-of-a-cicd-variable \"Learn more\")\\n\\nAll (default) \\n\\n  *   *   * * \\n  *   * \\n1 result \\n* * * *\\n\\n* Enter a search query to find more environments, or use * to create a wildcard. \\n\\nVisibility \\n\\n<::before><::after> Visible \\n\\nCan be seen in job logs. \\n\\n<::before><::after> Masked \\n\\nMasked in job logs but value can be revealed in CI/CD settings. Requires values to meet regular expressions requirements. \\n\\n<::before><::after> Masked and hidden \\n\\nMasked in job logs, and can never be revealed in the CI/CD settings after the variable is saved. \\n\\nFlags  [ ](/help/ci/variables/index#define-a-cicd-variable-in-the-ui \"Define a CI/CD variable in the UI\")\\n\\n<::before><::after> Protect variable \\n\\nExport variable to pipelines running on protected branches and tags only. \\n\\n<::before><::after> Expand variable reference \\n\\n` $ ` will be treated as the start of a reference to another variable. \\n\\nDescription  (optional) \\n\\nThe description of the variable\\'s value or usage. \\n\\nKey \\n\\n  *   * \\n\\n\\nYou can use CI/CD variables with the same name in different places, but the variables might overwrite each other. [ What is the order of precedence for variables? ](/help/ci/variables/index#cicd-variable-precedence)\\n\\nValue \\n\\nSave changes  Delete variable  Cancel \\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  Pipeline trigger tokens \\n\\nTrigger a pipeline for a branch or tag by generating a trigger token and using it with an API call. The token impersonates a user\\'s project access and permissions. [ Learn more. ](/help/ci/triggers/index.md)\\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\n##  Active pipeline trigger tokens  0 \\n\\nReveal values  Add new token \\n\\n####  Add new pipeline trigger token \\n\\nIt is a security risk to save tokens in plain text in your project, or store them in a way that malicious users could access them. A leaked trigger token could be used to force an unscheduled deployment, attempt to access CI/CD variables, or other malicious uses. [ How can I keep my tokens secure? ](/help/security/tokens/index.md#security-considerations)\\n\\nDescription \\n\\nTrigger description is required. \\n\\nCreate pipeline trigger token  Cancel \\n\\nNo trigger tokens have been created yet. Add one using the form above. \\n\\n<::marker> View trigger token usage examples \\n\\nThese examples show common methods of triggering a pipeline with a pipeline trigger token. The URL and ID for this project is prefilled. \\n\\nIn each example, replace ` TOKEN ` with the trigger token you generated and replace ` REF_NAME ` with the branch or tag name. \\n\\n#####  Use cURL \\n    \\n    \\n    curl -X POST \\\\\\n         --fail \\\\\\n         -F token=TOKEN \\\\\\n         -F ref=REF_NAME \\\\\\n         http://the-agent-company.com:8929/api/v4/projects/15/trigger/pipeline\\n    \\n\\n#####  Use .gitlab-ci.yml \\n    \\n    \\n    script:\\n      - \"curl -X POST --fail -F token=TOKEN -F ref=REF_NAME http://the-agent-company.com:8929/api/v4/projects/15/trigger/pipeline\"\\n    \\n\\n#####  Use webhook \\n    \\n    \\n    http://the-agent-company.com:8929/api/v4/projects/15/ref/REF_NAME/trigger/pipeline?token=TOKEN\\n    \\n\\n#####  Pass job variables \\n\\nTo pass variables to the triggered pipeline, add ` variables[VARIABLE]=VALUE ` to the API request. \\n\\ncURL: \\n    \\n    \\n    curl -X POST \\\\\\n         --fail \\\\\\n         -F token=TOKEN \\\\\\n         -F \"ref=REF_NAME\" \\\\\\n         -F \"variables[RUN_NIGHTLY_BUILD]=true\" \\\\\\n         http://the-agent-company.com:8929/api/v4/projects/15/trigger/pipeline\\n    \\n\\nWebhook: \\n    \\n    \\n    http://the-agent-company.com:8929/api/v4/projects/15/ref/REF_NAME/trigger/pipeline?token=TOKEN&variables[RUN_NIGHTLY_BUILD]=true\\n    \\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  Deploy freezes \\n\\nAdd a freeze period to prevent unintended releases during a period of time for a given environment. You must update the deployment jobs in ` .gitlab-ci.yml ` according to the deploy freezes added here. [ Learn more. ](/help/user/project/releases/index.md#prevent-unintentional-releases-by-setting-a-deploy-freeze) Specify deploy freezes using [ cron syntax ](https://crontab.guru/) . \\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\n##  Deploy freezes  0 \\n\\nAdd deploy freeze \\n\\nFreeze start  |  Freeze end  |  Time zone  |  Actions   \\n---|---|---|---  \\nNo deploy freezes exist for this project. To add one, select Add deploy freeze above.   \\n  \\nExpand \\n\\n##  Job token permissions \\n\\nControl which projects can use CI/CD job tokens to authenticate with this project. \\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\nAuthorized groups and projects \\n\\nSelect the groups and projects authorized to use a CI/CD job token to authenticate requests to this project. [ Learn more ](/help/ci/jobs/ci_job_token#control-job-token-access-to-your-project) . \\n\\n<::before><::after> All groups and projects \\n\\n<::before><::after> Only this project and any groups and projects in the allowlist \\n\\nSave Changes \\n\\n##  CI/CD job token allowlist  0  1 \\n\\nEnsure only groups and projects with members authorized to access sensitive project data are added to the allowlist. \\n\\nAdd group or project \\n\\n|   \\n---|---  \\nI  [ root/internal-api-client ](/root/internal-api-client) |   \\n  \\n<::before>\\n\\nThe **Limit access** _**from** _ **this project** setting is deprecated and scheduled for removal in the 18.0 milestone. Use the **Authorized groups and projects** setting and allowlist instead. [ How do I do this? ](/help/ci/jobs/ci_job_token#limit-your-projects-job-token-access-deprecated)\\n\\nLimit access _from_ this project (Deprecated)  Prevent CI/CD job tokens from this project from being used to access other projects unless the other project is added to the allowlist. It is a security risk to disable this feature, because unauthorized projects might attempt to retrieve an active token and access the API. [ Learn more ](/help/ci/jobs/ci_job_token#limit-your-projects-job-token-access-deprecated) . **Disabling this feature is a permanent change.**\\n\\n##  Add an existing project to the scope  1 \\n\\nAdd project \\n\\n|   \\n---|---  \\nI  [ root/internal-api-client ](/root/internal-api-client) |   \\n  \\nExpand \\n\\n##  Secure files \\n\\nUse secure files to store files used by your pipelines such as Android keystores, or Apple provisioning profiles and signing certificates. [ Learn more ](/help/ci/secure_files/index.md)\\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\n##  Files  0 \\n\\nUpload File \\n\\nFile name  |  Uploaded date  |  Actions   \\n---|---|---  \\nThere are no secure files yet.   \\n  \\n<::before>\\n\\nEdit \\n', url='http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/internal-api-client/-/settings/ci_cd', trigger_by_action='browse_interactive', error=False, observation='browse', goal_image_urls=[], open_pages_urls=['http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/internal-api-client', 'http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/internal-api-client', 'http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/internal-api-client/-/settings/ci_cd'], active_page_index=2, last_browser_action=\"scroll(0, 800)\\nnoop(400)\\nclick('1460')\\nnoop(400)\\nscroll(0, 600)\\nnoop(300)\\nclick('1557')\\nnoop(1200)\", last_browser_action_error='', focused_element_bid='1557'), BrowseInteractiveAction(browser_actions=\"click('1932')\\nnoop(300)\\nclick('1979')\\nnoop(1200)\", thought='', browsergym_send_msg_to_user='', action='browse_interactive', security_risk=None), BrowserOutputObservation(content='Skip to main content \\n\\n##  Primary navigation \\n\\n[ Homepage  ](/)\\n\\nCreate new... \\n\\n  * In this project \\n\\n    * [ New issue  ](/root/internal-api-client/-/issues/new)\\n    * [ New merge request  ](/root